cff-version: 1.2.0
# Root citation file. GitHub renders its "Cite this repository" widget ONLY from a
# CITATION.cff at the repository root, so the detailed per-project file at
# projects/perturb-seq-eval/CITATION.cff is invisible to that UI. This file exists to
# surface it: it cites the repository as software and names the published paper as the
# PREFERRED citation, which is the CFF idiom for "cite the paper, not the code".
#
# Deliberate omissions, so a later reader does not read them as oversights:
#   - no `license:` — the repository is MIXED-licence. README's License section: what the
#     author wrote in libs/, projects/ and research/MODELS.md is Apache-2.0, while the
#     cloned sub-repos keep their upstream licences (CC-BY-NC-4.0, MIT, Apache-2.0).
#     A single SPDX identifier here would be a false claim about the whole tree.
#   - no `email:` — ORCID identifies the author unambiguously and citation tooling does not
#     need an address. The per-project file already carries one; this does not add a copy.
#   - `preferred-citation` has NO `journal:` field. Zenodo is a repository, not a journal,
#     and the deposit is preprint-class. Naming it as a journal would overstate the venue.
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the paper under `preferred-citation`.
  The DOI there is the Zenodo CONCEPT DOI, which always resolves to the latest
  published version.
title: "bioFM — a living workspace for Biological Foundation Models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mo"
    given-names: "Mang-yin"
    affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-5233-3142"
repository-code: "https://github.com/supmo668/bioFM"
url: "https://github.com/supmo668/bioFM"
keywords:
  - biological foundation models
  - single-cell
  - perturb-seq
  - multi-agent
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: "Mo"
      given-names: "Mang-yin"
      affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-5233-3142"
  title: >-
    Does Agent Confidence Entropy Predict Task Difficulty? A Pre-registered,
    Provenance-Complete Test of Agentic Hyperparameter Tuning for Perturb-seq
    Response Prediction
  year: 2026
  month: 10
  doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19716140"
  url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19716140"
  license: "CC-BY-4.0"
  notes: >-
    Preprint-class deposit archived on Zenodo (concept DOI; resolves to v0.6.0,
    published 2026-10-16). The same release is deposited on Figshare as
    10.6084/m9.figshare.32086920.v6, and the two records reference each other —
    the Zenodo record carries `isIdenticalTo` to the Figshare DOI. Full version
    lineage v1..v6 and every superseded DOI are documented in
    projects/perturb-seq-eval/CITATION.cff.
